  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nTemperatures are expected to drop to near or below freezing\nthrough the morning, with a Freeze Warning in effect. Frost, \nand even a few freezing temperatures are likely again tonight, \nthough it is possible the growing season could end if a \nwidespread freeze occurs this morning. \n\nOtherwise, model ensembles indicate a closed low should remain \noff of the Mid Atlantic/Carolina coast region through most of \nthe week, with a trough across the western CONUS. In between \nthese two systems, a ridge is progged to persist across the \ncentral CONUS to the Upper Ohio Valley region through the \nupcoming week. This should maintain dry weather across the \narea, with near seasonable temperatures. A weak trough is \nprogged to cross the area on the NE periphery of the ridge on \nThursday, though with surface high pressure in place only a \nslight decrease in temperature is expected by late week with the\nlower 500mb heights.",
